WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- What's up y'all,

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.250
I'm here with Kate
Flannery and Joel McHale!

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:04.526
Give it up for 'em, y'all.

00:00:04.526 --> 00:00:05.600
(crowd cheering)
(audience member whistling)

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.960
In honor of St. Patrick's
Day in all its green glory,

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.610
it's time for a game called
Things That Are Green.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.688
Kate--
(Irish jig music)

00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:15.851
♪ Things that are green ♪

00:00:15.851 --> 00:00:16.880
- Nice job, band.
- I didn't actually know

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.980
that was going, but nicely done.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.271
- That interruption was

00:00:20.271 --> 00:00:21.179
from the band.
- Kate--

00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:22.177
(Kate and Kelly laughing)

00:00:22.177 --> 00:00:23.540
The band is awesome.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.240
Kate has graciously
agreed to host the game

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.740
while I destroy Joel.
(Joel mock laughs)

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.870
So tell us the rules, Kate.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:30.703
- Okay, the rules.

00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:32.980
I'm gonna ask you questions
about green things.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:33.994
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:33.994 --> 00:00:34.827
- If you hit the buzzer first--

00:00:34.827 --> 00:00:35.660
- Yes. (giggles)

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.070
- You get the question
right, you get a point.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.050
- Yes.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.381
- Don't hit me, hit the buzzer.

00:00:39.381 --> 00:00:40.214
(Kelly giggles)
- Okay.

00:00:40.214 --> 00:00:42.970
- If you're wrong, the
other person can steal.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:46.090
We also have refreshing,
healthy detox green drinks

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.690
to replenish you after your day of booze.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.523
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:49.523 --> 00:00:51.410
- Kelly is playing for the lasses

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.140
in our house seats.
(audience claps)

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.970
Joel is playing for the lads.
(audience member whoops)

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.850
The winner gets a cool green prize.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:00:59.683
- Yes.
- You ready?

00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:00.548
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:01:00.548 --> 00:01:01.381
- [Joel] All right,

00:01:01.381 --> 00:01:02.214
this is exciting.
- Okay, question number one.

00:01:02.214 --> 00:01:03.215
- [Kelly] Okay!

00:01:03.215 --> 00:01:04.048
(gentle quiz music)

00:01:04.048 --> 00:01:05.310
- What's the lucky meadow weed

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.031
that also is a symbol
for St. Patrick's Day?

00:01:08.031 --> 00:01:09.210
(Joel grunts)

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.300
- Four leaf clover!

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.133
(bell dings)

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:11.986
- [Joel] Wrong!

00:01:11.986 --> 00:01:12.819
(audience cheers)
- You're gonna have to

00:01:12.819 --> 00:01:14.100
come with it, I'm just saying.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.200
- No, it's a dandelion.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.472
- She's bringing it.
- It's a dandelion (laughs).

00:01:17.472 --> 00:01:18.305
(audience member chuckles)

00:01:18.305 --> 00:01:19.260
- All right, question two.
(gentle quiz music)

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.241
Who were the heroes in a half--

00:01:21.241 --> 00:01:23.060
Who were the heroes in a half shell?

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.852
- I didn't even--
- Ninja turtles!

00:01:24.852 --> 00:01:25.685
(bell dings)

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.279
You said heroes in a half shell.

00:01:27.279 --> 00:01:28.112
(audience claps)
I was a ninja turtle fan.

00:01:28.112 --> 00:01:29.799
Were you a ninja turtle--
- I was not ready.

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:31.480
- [Kelly] Sorry.
- You were in a band,

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.313
a ninja turtle band?
- I took a breath.

00:01:32.313 --> 00:01:34.656
(Kelly laughs)
Wait, wait, wait.

00:01:34.656 --> 00:01:35.580
(Kelly laughing loudly)
You were in a band

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.750
that dressed up as ninja turtles?

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.406
- No, I was a Ninja turtle fan.

00:01:39.406 --> 00:01:40.446
- Oh, okay.

00:01:40.446 --> 00:01:41.404
That's different.

00:01:41.404 --> 00:01:42.237
- But now I want to start a band.

00:01:42.237 --> 00:01:43.128
Will y'all be in it?

00:01:43.128 --> 00:01:44.794
- Sure. I'm gonna be Raphael.
- I'll be in it.

00:01:44.794 --> 00:01:45.710
I'll be Michelangelo.
- Yeah.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:46.640
- Woo-hoo!
- I wanna be, Michel--

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:47.473
Fine, Donatello.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:48.474
- I'll be Keith Haring.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.206
(everybody laughing)
- I can see that.

00:01:50.206 --> 00:01:51.740
(gentle quiz music)
- What green vegetable

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.010
will make your pee smell funny?

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.390
- Oh, I got that one.
(Kelly giggles)

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:57.608
Asparagi.

00:01:57.608 --> 00:01:58.770
(bell dings)
- Asparagi!

00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.603
- Oh, thank you.

00:01:59.603 --> 00:02:01.228
(audience claps)
- Number four.

00:02:01.228 --> 00:02:03.400
(gentle quiz music)
Who had a pig

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.910
for a girlfriend and sang,
It's Not Easy Being Green?

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:07.898
- [Kelly] Oh, oh!

00:02:07.898 --> 00:02:08.950
Dang.

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.380
- Kermit the Frog, everybody.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.213
(bell dings)
- Nice.

00:02:12.213 --> 00:02:13.577
- Oh, this one's really good.
- We are tied, it's nice.

00:02:13.577 --> 00:02:14.825
- This one's really good.
- We're tied.

00:02:14.825 --> 00:02:15.820
It's all tied up here on
the Kelly Clarkson show.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.540
- [Joel] Hold on a second,
I just wanna take a sip.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.703
- Okay.
- All right, refresh yourself.

00:02:18.703 --> 00:02:19.785
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:19.785 --> 00:02:23.343
(laughs loudly) I'll get around
it, don't you even worry.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:25.623
- Wait, okay.
- Okay.

00:02:25.623 --> 00:02:27.893
It's the producers who
got more nervous than...

00:02:27.893 --> 00:02:28.726
(Kate laughs)

00:02:28.726 --> 00:02:30.061
Than when I brought a lamb on stage.

00:02:30.061 --> 00:02:30.894
(Kate and Kelly laughing)

00:02:30.894 --> 00:02:31.727
- I'm so ready.
(gentle quiz music)

00:02:31.727 --> 00:02:32.940
- Okay, question number five.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.853
Who was the most adorable
character in The Mandalorian?

00:02:35.853 --> 00:02:38.230
(Joel grunts)
- Oh!

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:39.880
- The Child.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:40.912
- [Kelly] No!

00:02:40.912 --> 00:02:41.745
(wrong answer buzzer)
- In The Mandalorian,

00:02:41.745 --> 00:02:42.578
that's the Baby Yoda.

00:02:42.578 --> 00:02:43.411
- [Kelly] No, Baby Yoda!

00:02:43.411 --> 00:02:44.289
- Yeah, that's called The Child.

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:45.122
- No, you said The Child!

00:02:45.122 --> 00:02:46.190
- It's called The Child.
- It's Baby Yoda!

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.302
- Baby Yoda's called The Child!

00:02:48.302 --> 00:02:50.137
- Baby Yoda!
- Can we check it?

00:02:50.137 --> 00:02:51.067
(audience laughs)

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:52.027
- [Crew Member] It's called The Child.

00:02:52.027 --> 00:02:53.827
- [Kelly] Oh, I thought it was Baby Yoda.

00:02:53.827 --> 00:02:54.660
(audience laughs)

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.500
Damn it, damn it, damn it!
(bell dings)

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.333
- Mm!

00:02:58.333 --> 00:02:59.300
- [Kate] All right, question number six.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.579
- Yes.
- Mm-hmm.

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:01.520
(gentle quiz music)
- Who's an ogre

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.370
who lived in a swamp and
had a best friend named--

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:04.354
- Shrek!

00:03:04.354 --> 00:03:05.187
(bell dings)

00:03:05.187 --> 00:03:06.496
- All right!

00:03:06.496 --> 00:03:07.336
- Dang it.
- That's right.

00:03:07.336 --> 00:03:08.776
That's right, Baby Yoda.
- Okay, we are tied.

00:03:08.776 --> 00:03:10.603
Ladies and gentlemen, we are tied.

00:03:10.603 --> 00:03:12.106
- (groans) I was gonna say Howie Mandel.

00:03:12.106 --> 00:03:13.720
- (laughs) What?
(audience chuckles)

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:14.739
- Darn it!

00:03:14.739 --> 00:03:16.340
(gentle quiz music)
- Question seven.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.940
Name a yellow fruit that you often buy

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:21.890
from the grocery store when it's green.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:22.723
- I got that.
- I don't know.

00:03:22.723 --> 00:03:23.556
- Who got that?

00:03:23.556 --> 00:03:24.794
- No.
- Kelly.

00:03:24.794 --> 00:03:26.474
- What, no, because
you're the producer here!

00:03:26.474 --> 00:03:28.100
(Kelly giggles)
(audience laughs)

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.584
The answer's Howie Mandel.

00:03:29.584 --> 00:03:30.740
(Kelly laughs)
(wrong answer buzzer)

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:31.590
- What is the answer?

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:32.810
If you know it, I'll give it to you.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:33.643
- [Joel] Are you serious?

00:03:33.643 --> 00:03:34.591
- Yeah.

00:03:34.591 --> 00:03:35.424
- A banana.

00:03:35.424 --> 00:03:36.257
- Okay.
(bell dings)

00:03:36.257 --> 00:03:37.090
- [Joel] Oh, okay.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:37.923
(gentle quiz music)
- Question eight.

00:03:37.923 --> 00:03:38.756
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:03:38.756 --> 00:03:40.980
- Who had a house dropped on her?

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.196
- Green, the Wicked Witch of the West!

00:03:42.196 --> 00:03:43.076
(Joel groans)
(bell dings)

00:03:43.076 --> 00:03:43.909
Whoo!

00:03:45.046 --> 00:03:45.879
Boom!

00:03:45.879 --> 00:03:46.850
- The tie breaker!

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:47.683
- [Kelly] Tie breaker.

00:03:47.683 --> 00:03:49.122
- Get serious!

00:03:49.122 --> 00:03:50.265
Come on, Joel.
- Hold on.

00:03:50.265 --> 00:03:51.098
Let me get my ringer.
- Come on,

00:03:51.098 --> 00:03:52.080
put your flask down.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.510
For once in your life.
- Okay.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.378
- [Kate] 'Kay.

00:03:54.378 --> 00:03:55.456
♪ For once in my life ♪

00:03:55.456 --> 00:03:56.289
(gentle quiz music)
- The last one

00:03:56.289 --> 00:03:59.090
is worth five points because
it's in limerick form.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:03:59.923
- Oh, geez.
- Okay, yes.

00:03:59.923 --> 00:04:02.650
- Okay, his power was actually rad.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.360
He fought all the guys who were bad.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.400
By turning real green
and getting real mean

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.768
whenever he got really mad.

00:04:09.768 --> 00:04:10.601
- Hulk!

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:11.898
(bell dings)
I just watched it!

00:04:11.898 --> 00:04:13.800
(audience cheers)
I just watched End Game!

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.549
Whoo!
- There's like twelve of them!

00:04:15.549 --> 00:04:16.628
Which one?

00:04:16.628 --> 00:04:19.309
- I said End Game!
- Kelly, Kelly, Kelly!

00:04:19.309 --> 00:04:21.709
We got a winner, ladies and gentlemen!

00:04:21.709 --> 00:04:22.542
(uplifting orchestral music)
- It's so sad

00:04:22.542 --> 00:04:23.520
that you're not gonna be on

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.040
Blake Shelton's Wall of
Champions because you're not one.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.104
(giggles)
(audience laughs)

00:04:29.104 --> 00:04:30.740
- You know what, that's fine.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:31.920
I'm going on Donahue.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.330
(Kelly cackles)

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.490
That's fine.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.709
- Let me--
- I've got another booking.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:40.997
- (laughs) That means all the
lasses in our house seats win.

00:04:40.997 --> 00:04:41.960
(audience claps)
But hell,

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.480
it's not easy being green, everybody.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.750
That's our joke for today.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.567
So let's say everyone's a winner.

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:48.167
(imitates air horn)

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.807
- This is good, right?
(Joel laughs)

00:04:50.807 --> 00:04:53.130
- The Nama Cold Press Juicer is one of the

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.970
strongest juicers on the market.

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:57.760
With up to 60% more juice,
The Nama is engineered

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.080
to provide more nutrients
and better flavor.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.360
It has multiple functions,

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.600
so you can make almond milk, which I love.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.110
Oat milk, and even sorbets,

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.570
or even green drinks like these.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.630
This is my personal favorite, whatever.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.780
Plus it's kid safe and super easy to clean

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.460
which is what every mom wants to hear.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.810
You're all going to get
a chance to start juicing

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.180
because everyone in our house seats

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:17.569
is getting a Nama Juicer!

00:05:17.569 --> 00:05:18.780
(imitates air horn)

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:20.025
(audience cheers)
(Joel laughs)

